A||N||23||Simon Hudson||difference between formula and GT Fiero||||1||
Z||000000||Simon Hudson||02-28-2001||12:20 AM||||What is the difference?  I can see the body style difference but what else?  suspension? engine? interior? etc.<P>Thanks,<P>Simon Hudson||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||02-28-2001||12:25 AM||||Mechanically the same, but certain options weren't available on Formula's and certain options were standard on GT's.<P>Also the seats were different on the GT's (much much much more durable on 88 GT's)<p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 02-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hank is Here||02-28-2001||12:26 AM||||Well the Formula was only made in 88 so yes under the skin (or plastic) they are the same.  Generally speaking the Formula's have less options (like no power mirrors)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||02-28-2001||07:19 PM||||Yup.  The Formula is a GT except for the body style and option content.  Same suspension and drivetrain.  To me, the Formula represents the truest Fiero. It's the suspension they originally designed, with the original body (with minor changes) and they were originally planning for a v6, even though it wasn't introduced until later.  The Formula is the Fiero that should have been released in 1984.  Had that been the case, the car may have fared better (Corvette people not withstanding).  Don't get me wrong, I love all Fieros, but I have a special place in my heart (and garage!) for Formulas.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000004||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||03-01-2001||04:51 PM||||The Formula is lighter than a GT by at least 100lbs.<P>So, the Formulas are the fastest stock Fieros 0 to 60.  <P>I agree with the previous post, the Formula is the Fiero they should have started with.<P>However, a Quad 4 5 spd Fiero would have been even better in the handling department.  Too bad the GM divisions don't work together.  The stupidity of competition within a company seems so obvious to me.  It's even called "divisions."<P>On the other hand, Chevorolet is a company that can never learn.  I will never buy another car with a bow tie on it.  I had a '93 Cavalier z24 once, and it broke constantly.<P>The dealer would say "what do you care, it's all going to be fixed under warranty . . ."<P>Those Chevy people just don't get it, do they?  Don't condem GM, for Buicks are some the highest quality american cars out there.<P>It's just stupid chevy that is messing up everything for GM.  They should just shut up and stop screwing with the other divisions.  Saturn, Oldsmobile, and Pontiac have all suffered under the jealousy of big stupid Chevy.  Chevy sucks and I hate them for any involvement they may have had in the demise of the Fiero.  I will not get over it.<P>I swear I will never own another Chevy.  I hope to live to see the division disappear.<P>Yes, Corvettes are nice cars.  But for $50K, they are a far cry from the quality and refinement of the Porsches and BMWs they compete with.  Chevy forgot that the Corvette was a low-buck supercar.  Now it's just an overpriced stupid car in my opinion.<P>Who could pass on a Boxster and buy a 'vette?<BR>Can you believe Chevy would even try to take on Porsche?  They are more stupid than a 1975 Nova looks.  Without question, chevy builds the lowest quality, worst looking cars that GM sells.<P>Ever hear the phrase "Bitchin' Camaro"?  Hint: it ain't no compliment . . .<BR><p>[This message has been edited by LuckyTheyWereEverMade (edited 03-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black88GT||03-01-2001||05:13 PM||||Hmm I'm no Corvette fan but you have to give it more credit then that.  It is a great car.  Everything Pontiac makes nowadays looks the same.  Personally I like they way they look but still, they look the same.  You can't really compare Chevy to Pontiac anyway.<P>I think blaming the Corvette for the demise of the Fiero is a big excuse.  It was GM/Pontiac's fault in the first place to not push for the '88 model year or better back in '82 or '83.  They sealed their own fate really.  They could have made the best car in '88, and spent millions on advertising, but it still wouldn't have changed sales significantly, because reputation is a much more powerful force then any of the other factors involved.  Why do you think so many people sware up and down they will never buy an american car again?  After the late 70s and 80s american cars got a bad rap for quality/reliability so now many people refuse to buy them no matter what.  <P>Remember, the common consumer isn't too bright.  Most of them do not buy vehicles because they are the best car/truck/SUV, they buy them because they are "cute" or they have to "keep up with the Jones' who just got an SUV too".  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Will||03-01-2001||07:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LuckyTheyWereEverMade:<BR><B>The Formula is lighter than a GT by at least 100lbs.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What's your source for that number?<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>Yes, Corvettes are nice cars.  But for $50K, they are a far cry from the quality and refinement of the Porsches and BMWs they compete with.  Chevy forgot that the Corvette was a low-buck supercar.  Now it's just an overpriced stupid car in my opinion.<P>Who could pass on a Boxster and buy a 'vette?<BR>Can you believe Chevy would even try to take on Porsche?  They are more stupid than a 1975 Nova looks.  Without question, chevy builds the lowest quality, worst looking cars that GM sells.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I could pass up a boxster for a Z06 Vette. The Vette is more like $45K and eats the Boxster for breakfast in performance. I haven't driven one, but nothing of what I have read about the C5 says anything about lack of refinement or lack of quality.<BR>Boxster S: 2855 lbs, 250 HP, $50,200, Strut (WTF?!) suspension all around, 18mpg city, 26 hwy.<BR>Corvette Z06: 3115 lbs, 385 HP, $47,855, Short-Long A-arm suspension all around, 19 mpg city, 28 hwy.<BR>The 'Vette has better road holding, slalom, and braking numbers than the Boxster. You bet I'd buy a Vette before a Boxster. Then I'd take the $2300 dollars I saved, go for a heads and cam package, and start hunting 911 Turbos.||||reg||1
Z||000007||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||03-01-2001||11:57 PM||||Who's blaming the corvette for the demise of Pontiac's Fiero?<P>I'm blaming Chevy.  They interfere in the business of all the other GM divisions.  They have tried to protect the Corvette from all internal competition.  Soon, Cadys will be giving the 'vette a run for it's money.  I hope they win.  <P>There is no denying that the Z06 has unbelievable performance.  But it's really, really, really, really ugly.  The hatchback 'vettes are a lot better looking.  But, they are no where near as refined and classy as the Boxster.  Remember, we are spending $50K . . .  <P>Regardless of the merits of corvettes, where similar models are produced by GM's other divisions, chevys have the poorest quality.  Buicks and Cadillacs are the best.<P>Regardless of how many cars I can beat with a 'vette, I wish nothing to do with them.  They do nothing for me.  I would say the same of any mustang including the Saleens.  But, I would jump at the chance to drive a Boxster.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||03-01-2001||11:57 PM||||Who's blaming the corvette for the demise of Pontiac's Fiero?<P>I'm blaming Chevy.  They interfere in the business of all the other GM divisions.  They have tried to protect the Corvette from all internal competition.  Soon, Cadys will be giving the 'vette a run for it's money.  I hope they win.  <P>There is no denying that the Z06 has unbelievable performance.  But it's really, really, really, really ugly.  The hatchback 'vettes are a lot better looking.  But, they are no where near as refined and classy as the Boxster.  Remember, we are spending $50K . . .  <P>Regardless of the merits of corvettes, where similar models are produced by GM's other divisions, chevys have the poorest quality.  Buicks and Cadillacs are the best.<P>Regardless of how many cars I can beat with a 'vette, I wish nothing to do with them.  They do nothing for me.  I would say the same of any mustang including the Saleens.  But, I would jump at the chance to drive a Boxster.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||G-Nasty||03-02-2001||12:32 AM||||Chevy CORSICA and CHEVETTE, Two of the worst cars ever conceived. That dude that went off in a rant is absolutely right- Chevy is a disgrace in technology application. I think the Z06 is actually made in JAPAN! Vettes are allright. Vipers and Fiero GT's still dominate GT series races. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||elfiero||03-02-2001||10:36 AM||||sounds like "lucky"just might be a frustrated<BR>yuppie wanna be-with a little too much<BR>starbucks thrown in.a pooorsha ain't nothing<BR>more than a high buck VW.like it or not,GM<BR>as a whole and pontiac in particular,would<BR>not exsist if not for the big bowtie!all of<BR>the bolt-on stuff for yer fiero CAME from<BR>chevy!(drive train,susp.ect)now lets all bow<BR>and beg forgivness to the gods at chevrolet!<BR>P.S.an "iron duke" is a redone '62 chevyII<BR>engine-or-1/2 of a SBC!!!||||reg||6
Z||000011||Will||03-02-2001||10:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by G-Nasty:<BR><B>Chevy CORSICA and CHEVETTE, Two of the worst cars ever conceived. That dude that went off in a rant is absolutely right- Chevy is a disgrace in technology application. I think the Z06 is actually made in JAPAN! Vettes are allright. Vipers and Fiero GT's still dominate GT series races. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hahahahahahahahahahahahahaha!!!!!<P>That's great. You should take that act on the road! Have you ever heard of Bowling Green, Kentucky? Z06 made in Japan! Hahaha!<P>Show me where you heard that Fieros dominate GT races.<P>Technology disgrace? GM uses the same engines across all platforms. If it's true of Chevy, its true of the rest of GM. The LS1/6 is one of the most technologically advanced engines anywhere. The LS1/6 PCM uses a 32 bit processor. Lamborghini doesn't even use 32 bit processors yet.<BR>The base engine on the Cavalier uses roller rockers and roller lifters ans sequential injection, the optional engine is a 2.4 twincam, descended from the Quad 4. The Cavalier has standard ABS, stainless steel exhaust, A/C, and power steering. For $13700. Technology disgrace? What planet are you from?<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>Regardless of the merits of corvettes, where similar models are produced by GM's other divisions, chevys have the poorest quality. Buicks and Cadillacs are the best.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's the way it's supposed to be. That's why Chevies are cheap and Buick doesn't make Cavaliers. The quality hierarchy is supposed to go like this: Chevrolet, Pontiac, Oldsmobile, Buick, Cadillac. Exactly the same way a Mercury is a nicer car than a Ford, even thought he two may be built on the same chassis.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Will||03-02-2001||11:01 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LuckyTheyWereEverMade:<BR>There is no denying that the Z06 has unbelievable performance.  But it's really, really, really, really ugly.  The hatchback 'vettes are a lot better looking.  But, they are no where near as refined and classy as the Boxster.  Remember, we are spending $50K . . .  <BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Define "refined" and "classy". All the reviews I have read said that the Vette is one of the easiest cars in the world to drive at 10/10ths. Doesn't that speak volumes about refinement?<BR>What exactly defines "class"?<P>There are two 'Vette body styles: Coupe/Z06/(formerly hardtop), and Convertible. There is no "hatchback".<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Regardless of how many cars I can beat with a 'vette, I wish nothing to do with them.  They do nothing for me.  I would say the same of any mustang including the Saleens.  But, I would jump at the chance to drive a Boxster.<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Then I guess you should learn to appreciate the visual appeal of Corvette tail lights, even when the road gets twisty.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Black88GT||03-02-2001||11:54 AM||||To say the Z06 is a bad car because it is ugly in your opinion is ludicrous.  I have had people try to say the same thing about Fiero's.  Your the first person I have ever heard call any model of the C5 ugly, you seem to be the very tiny minority there.  There are people that think Ferrari 360 Modena's are ugly too so you can't please everyone.<P>The Boxster is ugly IMHO, and I would rather have a C5 'vette any day.<P>Will, I think he calls it classy because its a Porsche.  Kinda silly to pick a car because of that but people do it all the time (i.e rich people).  <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/af.bmp"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Raydar||03-02-2001||12:16 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>...Your the first person I have ever heard call any model of the C5 ugly, you seem to be the very tiny minority there.  There are people that think Ferrari 360 Modena's are ugly too so you can't please everyone.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think the rear view (the one most people are likely to see)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> of the C5 is a bit strange looking.<BR> <BR>"I like my sports cars like I like my women."<BR>"Fine. Get in your big-ass Corvette and get outta here."<P>From other angles, I think it looks great.<BR>And it nearly always wins the automotive mags' "bang for the buck" contests.<P>360 Modena? I'll take one. Any day. Any time.<BR>One of the most beautiful cars I've ever seen. Kinda has lines that resemble a Fiero. <P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 03-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||b lo 0||03-02-2001||01:07 PM||||quote:<BR>The Formula is lighter than a GT by at least 100lbs.<P>                          So, the Formulas are the fastest stock Fieros 0 to 60. <P>WRONG!!  '85 GT's were-same wieght as Formulas (notchbacks, remember?) and 145 factory HP as opposed to 135 for '86-'88 V6s.  +10 hp and same weight means FASTER!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">     <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!<P><A HREF="http://clubs.excite.com/welcome/main?cid=.zXb1DJ1lsCL&aid=22&auth=" TARGET=_blank>Pontiac Fiero Owner's Club</A>-Pics, Videos and More-Or Post your Own||||reg||1
Z||000016||WKDFIRO||03-02-2001||01:21 PM||||Fieros, specificly the Super Duty Fieros, dominated the GTU (UNDER 3.0 liters) class of racing back in the day. Finally resting the title from the seemingly unbeatable RX-7. Another version even competed in the GTP class with some good results, but things were already starting to wind down...<P>Fiero by Gary Witzenberg||||reg||1
Z||000017||mrfiero||03-02-2001||02:27 PM||||I don't want to start another debate about this, but ALL V-6 Fiero engines are the same (sans the '88 being internally balanced).  <P>The horsepower rating for the '85 was actually 140, not 145 and it was taken at a higher RPM than the later years.  This was done for emissions purposes only.....the later V-6's produce the same amount of power as an '85.  <P>As far as which is faster......it depends on who is driving what.  Both will be very close in acceleration, so I think the point is moot. ||||reg||1
Z||000018||rockcrawl||03-02-2001||02:29 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>145 factory HP as opposed to 135 for '86-'88 V6s<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The 85 2.8 was not any more powerful than the 87-88s. The 85-86s were factory rated at 140hp and the 87-88s were rated 135hp. The 87-88s were tested at a different RPM for emmisions reasons, that's why the HP numbers are different. The 88 also had an internally ballanced crank and lighter pistons. There has been some discussion about the '85 having a superior ECM, but I'm not sure how true that is.<P>mrfiero, you beat me to it!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by rockcrawl (edited 03-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||Alex4mula||03-02-2001||02:34 PM||||There are 3 bodys for the C5: Coupe, Hard Top and convertible. Porshe Boxter's are nice upscale VW. When I bought my C5 I took a look at the boxter. Very easy to decide. No storage place in the VW, oops, I mean the Boxter. Power?? Who said the Boxter was a powerful car then (98)? Even now? C5 are in a different category in that respect. I personaly like both body styles (to each his own) but would choose the C5 anytime over almost any Porshe.||||reg||1
Z||000020||DRH||03-02-2001||06:42 PM||||Don't you have to shift into 3rd to hit 60 (without redlining) in a 5 speed but not in a 4 speed? Seems like the time lost shifting might give the 85 4 speed a slight advantage in 0-60.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000021||G-Nasty||03-02-2001||09:35 PM||||It was a joke WILL...I Know Z06's are made here but it is obvious Japan has high quality control and higher tech cars (*double wishbone Supra Nsx etc. 4 valves per cylinder Vtech you get the idea). I've never seen a Fiero GT on a race track but if Gary says so then I believe him. AS of yet Viper GTSR Class continues to dominate both vettes and porsche. I did see C5 win a recent race on endurance. ||||reg||1
Z||000022||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||03-04-2001||05:15 AM||||Hmmm . . .<P>I am still trying to figure out how to buy the VW version of the Porsche Boxster everyone seems to be talking about.  Can anyone tell me which model of VW is mid-engined?<P>I can see that I have offended many Forum members with my opinion of the corvette.  For those, it may seem ironic that I grew up in a 'vette family (1966 427 4spd, 1977, and 1978 L82).  At the time, the vette looked like a futuristic super car.  Now, mid 70s vettes don't look so cool.<P>On the other hand a mid 70s porsche 911 is still a very cool car.  Remember when IROC camaros were a big deal?  Remember the Porsche 928 S 4?  What about the 911? There is a difference.<P>My affinity for the Boxster lies in it's mid engined layout.  That's the same reason I would choose a Lotus Esprit over the 'vette.  I do not contest that the Corvette has incredible performance.  It just looks like a chevy to me.<P>In 1984, the new 'vette was the best handling car (by lateral acceleration at least) that the average middle class guy could afford. Now, no one wants them because the ride is really harsh.  It's hard to know which Corvette will be remembered as a good one. <P>There are very few Porsches that I do not want.  It's the same feeling I have for my Fiero.  Though any Mustang GT can waste my 2M4 in any category (except MPG), I don't want to drive a front engine V8 with a rear live axle.  It's not fun unless the pavement is flat, dry, and clear.  The best mountain roads are bumpy wet and poorly maintained.  <P>I once had one of the 89 Dodge colt GTs, "the fastest colts ever made" as Dodge claimed when I bought it new.  My friend in college had an '92 MR2 Turbo that was yellow.  There was a second friend with a red '93 Mazda RX7 turbo (unbelievable car!).  Though their cars were much better performers than my colt, my friends were not skilled enough to drive them that way.  They could never keep up with my colt.  Why?<P>I never had to lift my foot off the gas, so the 120HP 2000lb colt 16-valve turbo was the perfect match for my level of driving skill.<P>I am not Mario Andretti.  For the 'vette owners and afficianados I have offended, I can only say that my opinion is that I would be faster and have more fun in the Boxster.<P>If you beat me with a 'vette, I won't cry.  I would still have my Boxster.  This is hypothetical of course, as my other cars are a Ford Ranger 4cyl/auto, and a Kawasaki KLR650.  <P>It is the same deal with my 2M4.  Every vette has to race it (talk about needing an ego boost).  Usually they have a stick and they can't drive it.  So, silly as this sounds, I get the jump on them every time.  By 40 MPH they are ahead of me, but who cares?  My car cost less than one of their payments.<P>When someone in a Ferrari or Porsche sees my 2M4 on the road, they smile and drive along with me.  I can't believe they even notice my little car.  To me, the engine in the back is just a dream come true.  It feels so different from any of the other cars I have driven.  <P>Someday, the Corvette will be mid-engined.  I suspect that I will change my mind when that day comes.  Until then, I am not waiting for Chevy to do what it has talked about for the last 15 to 20 years.    <P>And, if Chevy had anything to do with the demise of the Fiero, then I am just more disappointed in them.  <P>But don't take it too hard.  You don't even want to hear what I think of Chrysler.  I owned a 1980 Dodge Omni and a Dodge colt turbo (blew it's timing belt at 40K miles, though recalled Dodge refused to pay for any of the costs).  And how about Honda's "sir, you would have to die to get out of your lease so you must purchase $1,000,000 liability insurance. . ."  Boy did I prove American Honda Finance wrong!  <P>Enough said.  We are here to worship Fieros.  The Corvette Forum is bigger and more powerful than the Fiero Forum, but that does not mean it's better!<P>And, I definitely not a yuppy, I like to wrench on cars, drink Budweiser beer, and I hate coffee.  Starbucks is the evil empire. Microbrews are for sipping with your pinkie extended.   <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000023||bubbajoexx||03-04-2001||08:53 AM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ed-3.jpg">  <BR>you want to eat porsches and vettes try this one 1300lbs 400 hp 350 mid engine 1979 kelmark gt real fast<p>[This message has been edited by bubbajoexx (edited 03-06-2001).]||||reg||1
